# HPSim — GSD Phase 10: Four-Chapter Interactive Learning Experience

## Mission

Transform HPSim from a research dashboard into an immersive, four-chapter interactive science-learning experience.

Follow the supplied Claude design document,C:\Users\toshr\OneDrive\Desktop\Hari@Work\Shri Hari - Official Documents\IIT KGP\Meta Project\.planning\phases\10-beginner-ux-refinement-visual-design\10-Brainstorm , as the primary UX and narrative specification.

The four chapters are:

1. **The Defect** — Discover what a dislocation is and watch it move.
2. **The Wall** — Discover how grain boundaries interact with dislocations.
3. **More Walls, More Strength** — Discover how smaller grains make metals stronger.
4. **The Pattern Has a Name** — Discover the Hall–Petch relationship through the student's own simulation experiments.

The existing advanced research dashboard remains available through a persistent Research Mode entry point.

This is a substantial redesign of the beginner experience, not another collection of dashboard cards.

**Core design principle: Build intuition before equations. Let students discover what you want them to know.**

A student should experience the physical phenomenon first, understand the pattern second, and learn the mathematical equation last.

